      'annotations': dict({
        'destructiveHint': False,
        'idempotentHint': False,
        'openWorldHint': False,
        'readOnlyHint': False,
        'title': 'Upload document',
      }),
      'description': "Upload a file, sent as base64 content, to Paperless as a new document. The file's type is found from its content, never from its name: PDF, PNG, JPEG, GIF, TIFF, BMP, WebP, plain text and CSV (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OpenDocument and RTF only if Paperless runs Tika and Gotenberg). Metadata is given by name like in search_documents; an unknown or ambiguous name is an error and nothing is uploaded, and tags are never created. Custom field values are checked per data type. Paperless consumes the file later (OCR, matching, workflows), so the result holds the task_id and, with wait_seconds, the new document_id and web_url. Problems only consumption finds, such as a taken archive serial number, show as state failure with a message. Each call adds a document: uploading the same content again makes a second one on Paperless 3.x, there is no duplicate check.",
      'inputSchema': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
